HTTP status codes to cloud/system errors,  but understanding them quickly can save a lot of time....



✅ HTTP STATUS CODES


🟢 200 OK – Request was successful, everything is working...we like this! 😄

🆕 201 Created – Request succeeded and a new resource was created.

🚫 204 No Content – Request succeeded but nothing to return.

🔁 301 Moved Permanently – Resource has been permanently moved to a new URL.

🔄 302 Found – Temporary redirect to a different URL.

❗ 400 Bad Request – Client sent something invalid (e.g., malformed syntax).

🔒 401 Unauthorized – Request lacks valid authentication credentials.

⛔ 403 Forbidden – Credentials are valid, but user doesn’t have permission.

🔍 404 Not Found – Requested resource doesn’t exist on the server.

⏳ 408 Request Timeout – Server timed out waiting for the client request.

🚦 429 Too Many Requests – Client sent too many requests in a short period.

💥 500 Internal Server Error – Generic error from the server side.

🧱 502 Bad Gateway – Server received an invalid response from upstream.

🛑 503 Service Unavailable – Server is temporarily overloaded or down.

⏱️ 504 Gateway Timeout – Upstream server didn’t respond in time.



⚙️ SYSTEM / CLOUD ERRORS:


🔐 PermissionDenied – Authenticated, but lacks necessary permissions.

🚷 ConnectionRefused – Target server rejected the connection request.

⌛ ConnectionTimedOut – Target server didn’t respond within allowed time.

💾 DiskFull – Operation failed due to lack of disk space.

🧠 OutOfMemory – Application or service exceeded allocated memory.

❌ AuthFailure – Login/token/key-based authentication failed.

📈 InstanceLimitExceeded – Cloud quota limit reached for resource type.

🧩 DependencyError – Failure due to an issue in a required service/component.

⚠️ ServiceUnavailable – Cloud provider or app service is currently down or restarting.



Not all the codes out there though - just the ones you keep running into!
